From: isp <40058476+isprogrammer@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: wwan: qcom_bam_dmux: re-check pc_state under state_lock in pc_irq

bam_dmux_pc_irq() compares the line level with pc_state before taking
state_lock. The RX watchdog resyncs pc_state from the wire level under
state_lock (lost edge / stale edge). If the watchdog wins the lock for an
edge the handler is already processing, both of them toggle the ack for
the same edge and the modem asserts in its A2 power handshake.

Seen on UFI003 during a VoLTE call: "RX watchdog: PC line asserted while
pc_state=0 (lost edge), resyncing" followed 47 ms later by
"fatal error received: a2_power.c:3017:A2 Assertion Failed".

Re-check under the lock and leave an edge that was already handled alone.
---
--- a/drivers/net/wwan/qcom_bam_dmux.c	2026-11-02 22:09:32.765176860 +0000
+++ b/drivers/net/wwan/qcom_bam_dmux.c	2026-11-02 22:09:32.766176862 +0000
@@ -2105,6 +2105,19 @@
 		return IRQ_HANDLED;
 
 	mutex_lock(&dmux->state_lock);
+	/*
+	 * Re-check under state_lock. While this (nested, threaded) handler
+	 * waited for the lock, the RX watchdog can already have handled the
+	 * same edge: it sees the wire asserted (or low) with pc_state stale,
+	 * takes the lock first and resyncs -- which includes toggling the
+	 * ack. Acking the same edge a second time leaves the modem's A2
+	 * handshake one toggle off and it asserts (a2_power.c:3017 seen 47 ms
+	 * after a "lost edge, resyncing" during a voice call).
+	 */
+	if (new_state == READ_ONCE(dmux->pc_state)) {
+		mutex_unlock(&dmux->state_lock);
+		return IRQ_HANDLED;
+	}
 	if (new_state) {
 		WRITE_ONCE(dmux->pm_suspend_start_ns, 0);
 		WRITE_ONCE(dmux->pc_state, true);
